#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:5
#: e542e9060ade470786884e06ef306de6
msgid "Fuel Flow and Level Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:7
#: d7c689764a9e49709e5d0392492f6898
msgid "In firmware versions 4.0 and later, ArduPilot provides the ability to use fuel flow and level sensors, in addition to battery monitors. Pulse output fuel flow sensors, PWM output fuel level sensors, and analog output fuel level sensors are supported. Just as an analog battery monitor provides current flow measurements with the capacity status being computed by the autopilot, these sensors provide fuel use or level status measurements to enable the same reporting and monitoring for liquid fuel systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:10
#: db000560306446c0a80d1bc5419f3851
msgid "Fuel Flow Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:12
#: 9481c4e0310d49309e6ad72013c79ced
msgid "Fuel flow sensors that provide a pulse for each unit of consumed fuel, such as `this <https://www.btflowmeter.com/en/flow-meter-products/flow-meters-lowflow-flowmeters-low-flow-turbine-flow-meter-fuel-flow-meters-diesel-fuel-flow-meter-watermeters-paddlewheel-flow-meter-oil-flow-meter-oilflowmeter-waterflowmeter-water-meters-turbineflowmeter-oilflowmeter/mini-flowmeter-fch-mini-pp-series-chemical/fch-m-pp-30-lpm-97478169-lc.html>`__, shown below, can be used just like a battery would be in ArduPilot, with monitoring, display, failsafes, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:17
#: d0a5be7d91754f82b22b7f3702030adc
msgid "image courtesy `BIO-TECH <https://www.btflowmeter.com/home.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:19
#: 96e4d711e2e84558bc66b0aa95ea1634
msgid "The displays/logs/limits for amps and mAh consumed are now actually the liters/hour and milliliters consumed. The voltage will always report as 1.0V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:22
#: 5eba4a75a7a843699298655e3cf63957
msgid "Connecting to the Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:24
#: 62b1074ff38e44b6b863aa297d0afded
msgid "Any GPIO capable pin on the :ref:`autopilot<common-autopilots>` can be used to connect to the sensor's output. If it is an open-collector output, a 10kOhm external resistor pull-up to 3.3V will be required. For Pixhawk-style autopilots, any AUX pin can be used. For most other autopilots, an upper PWM output can be used. In either case, it must be freed up from use as a PWM output by setting the ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` lower than the total number of outputs available for PWM use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:27
#: bf1b692c22424f7d97a70b4ea1e2f2bf
msgid "in firmware versions 4.2 and later, the method for setting a PWM/SERVO/MOTOR output to be a GPIO function is changed. Instead of ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` being used, the individual ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` parameter is merely set to \"-1\". If set to \"0\", it remains a PWM output, unassigned to a function, and outputs that output's trim value when board safety is not active. If the servo function is being \"mirrored\" to a remote device, as in the case of a DroneCAN or KDECAN ESC, then in order to change the autopilot board's corresponding output pin to be a GPIO, but allow the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` to still be assigned to the remote device, the :ref:`SERVO_GPIO_MASK<SERVO_GPIO_MASK>` parameter can be used to assign the board pin to be a GPIO without affecting the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` assignment for the remote device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:29
#: b00090ba86404ff9aee00b83b5f63b7f
msgid "For example, if the board provides 6 outputs normally, setting ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` to 5 would make PWM output 6 available for use as a GPIO. The pin number assigned to that output when used as a GPIO needs to be determined from its hwdef.dat file, located `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef>`__ as shown below, where PWM6 is assigned as GPIO pin 55 when used as such:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:35
#: 788da5ba67fe45b8bda7657b3d6f3f9e
msgid "These sensors can sometimes provide erroneous data due to vibrations. This will cause the autopilot to assume that a higher amount of fuel has passed through the sensor than has been consumed from the tank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:38
#: c74d45ecb339433791a17939e5022360
msgid "Fuel Level Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:41
#: 0e0aef53e08b4241a671a08c956159c2
msgid "PWM Fuel Level Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:43
#: 51be5607cd2d4c368350827c2c5298d8
msgid "Fuel level sensors that output a PWM signal proportional to the level of fuel remaining in the tank such as the one supplied by `Foxtech <https://www.foxtechfpv.com/pwm-output-liquid-level-senser.html>`__ shown below are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:48
#: e5ea05e144fd459795e4b6192332d25d
msgid "The displays/logs/limits for mAh consumed are now actually the milliliters consumed with 1100 us PWM input indicating empty, and 1900 us PWM indicating full. The voltage will always report as 1.0V. The current is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:50
#: 0f4b95b1ed3f48f489a3dc7bf73bbdf7
msgid "Any GPIO-capable pin can be used as the PWM input from the sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:53
#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:80
#: 889bcfbd2bc246ff9c92b98caf5ba611
#: a67bac32e0404fd5a094ea764b0c5459
msgid "Parameter Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:55
#: d295ccbf96bd4a7f94cda2e4fc4933c3
msgid "Like analog battery current and capacity monitoring, the key parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:57
#: 52fe0a28e82644acb591385eaa724a9d
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` This sets the type of sensor. In this case, type 11 for pulse fuel flow sensors, and 12 for PWM fuel level sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:58
#: 83fa1ec652374915b0edb6469da7fdb6
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` This is the GPIO pin where the sensor is attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:59
#: cc5c12a3459747d0a4837de181ce0835
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` This is set in milliliters per pulse for fuel flow sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:60
#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:83
#: 337a30de0b444cd2b35f09c5b5194dfb
#: 454c7d1d1d164f9bb9845558da086fcf
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CAPACITY<BATT_CAPACITY>` This is the capacity in milliliters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:61
#: c75438f567624c6fa592bb04c420a1fd
msgid ":ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH<BATT_LOW_MAH>` This is set in milliliters instead of mAh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:62
#: 1363c265b9a1415c9f6bfd22084f10a3
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_MAH<BATT_CRT_MAH>` This is set in milliliters instead of mAh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:66
#: df7164fdc42d488d9ecfea105e80eb9b
msgid "Analog Fuel Level Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:68
#: d48f056b2dfa491ead2734d22a9ea92c
msgid "Fuel level sensors that output voltage are supported in ArduPilot version 4.3 and later. These types of sensors are also sometimes called fuel senders and are widely available from many manufacturers. Just as with the PWM type sensors, the estimated volume of fluid in the tank is shown as mAh when it is now actually milliliters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:70
#: 7186f33746d7463481051eb694f0e103
msgid "Any analog-capable pin can be used as the input from the sensor. Carefully consider the maximum voltage that the chosen ADC pin can measure and tolerate. Adding an external voltage divider might be necessary. To assist with calibrating these types of sensors, the voltage ArduPilot sees on the analog pin is shown in the battery voltage field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:72
#: fffda67b6f6e461c866f1bb3a60dbd2a
msgid "A low-pass filter feature is available to reduce the impact of tank slosh on the measured fuel level. The battery current field shows the voltage through the low-pass filter. The suggested range for the low-pass filter is between 0.2 Hz and 0.5 Hz. Setting the filter to a value of -1 will disable it and unfiltered voltage from the analog pin will be used. The filtered voltage value will be logged with a cutoff frequency of 0.3 Hz even when the filter is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:77
#: 9c89548fdfa74ba2bbcdd9fe6c71b363
msgid "This feature assumes linear fuel tank shapes and even distribution of fuel in the tank. It will not take into account non-uniform-shaped tanks or sloped fuel levels. This should be taken into consideration when setting failsafe values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:82
#: 1df0026497e742e9bcde0a768f02d81f
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` The sets the type of sensor. In this case, use type 24 for analog fuel level sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:84
#: 277de512c3174733aef52d1d69719c7f
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FL_VLT_MIN<BATT_FL_VLT_MIN>` This is the minimum voltage seen on the analog pin when the fuel tank is empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:85
#: 7517ff4a9f3b461bb4c356ce496de766
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FL_V_MULT<BATT_FL_V_MULT>` The is a multiplier calculated using the minimum and maximum voltage measured on the analog pin. This is calculated as 1 / (Voltage_Full - Voltage_Empty)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:86
#: 3f37a4278b0b4850b33617224f0d54f5
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FL_FLTR<BATT_FL_FLTR>` This is the frequency of the low pass filter in Hertz. A value of -1 disables the filter and unfiltered voltage is used to determine the fuel level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:87
#: d4cade0654af4944a5eaffe4d24f5ee6
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FL_PIN<BATT_FL_PIN>` This is the analog pin where the sensor is attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:90
#: 9b2d95d335664755b4e1c4a7cbca65c9
msgid "Advanced Parameter Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:92
#: 825df9d8b20b4637b45cad2cd05319c2
msgid "Fuel level is normally calculated using a linear relationship between fuel level and reported analog voltage from the sensor. However, some sensors have a non-linear output versus fuel level. ArduPilot provides up to a third order polynomial curve fit by changing the following parameters from their default values (which is a linear fit):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:94
#: d954b1f6987d41ad842c24a5304fd7f6
msgid "example shown for first battery monitor - :ref:`BATT_FL_FF<BATT_FL_FF>` First order polynomial fit term - :ref:`BATT_FL_FS<BATT_FL_FS>` Second order polynomial fit term - :ref:`BATT_FL_FT<BATT_FL_FT>` Third order polynomial fit term - :ref:`BATT_FL_OFF<BATT_FL_OFF>` Offset term"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:100
#: 1228ed6ed32844dca40e4f2f6d57c74e
msgid "every voltage sample from the sensor is modified as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:102
#: 7ee0f335c6a04240b3abbc62642451ba
msgid "measured sensor voltage = vm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:104
#: e1e2fd8a947f4515a58dde92a1f71d5e
msgid "modified voltage = (BATT_FL_FT * vm^3 + BATT_FL_FS * vm^2 + BATT_FL_FF * vm) + BATT_FL_OFF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:106
#: 483517bf99e542edb77175399cfd3112
msgid "This allows the non-linearity to be compensated. The values for these parameters should be obtained from the sensor manufacturer, if applicable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:109
#: 925f5f5fa9e449ee9a8f28c4c59323fe
msgid "Serial Port Sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:111
#: ecfdb3d7fc71404eabb9acc25db72f14
msgid "These send information about fuel flow via connection to a Serial port on the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fuel-sensors.rst:113
#: 201b8483d25e4e099ab5877ae66079b0
msgid "Currently, the `VSPeak flow meter <https://www.vspeak-modell.de/en/flow-meter>`__ is supported via a LUA script driver, `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/drivers/VSPeak_flow_meter.lua>`__. Setup information is contained it the script's `.md  file <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/drivers/VSPeak_flow_meter.md>`__."
msgstr ""
